[quote="Christopher"]

Wait, are you saying that Apostate is too easy?That&#39;s one I haven&#39;t heard before.

[/quote]

&nbsp;

Well yeah. &nbsp;I&#39;ve only played him once, so maybe that&#39;s part of it, but he really didn&#39;t seem to pose any threat at all. &nbsp;Lowest base HP of any villian (Other than the Dreamer who doesn&#39;t count, and Blade who also doesn&#39;t count because he gets a bonus 30 HP, and the Vengenance Villians who don&#39;t count), he never flips if you fight him intelligently, all you really have to do is whack his relics and demons, then kill him before he kills you (and even if you lose a hero along the way, They&#39;ll probably have an incapacitated power that really screws with his cards). &nbsp;

[quote="Pinecone3"]

 Well yeah. &nbsp;I&#39;ve only played him once, so maybe that&#39;s part of it, but he really didn&#39;t seem to pose any threat at all. &nbsp; 

[/quote]

What&nbsp;cmschex said above holds a lot of truth to it. Apostate most of the time will be a fairly easy fight in my experience, and his Advanced Mode doesn&#39;t change him in any meaningful way really (relic spirits are easily ignored). But every once in a while you see exactly how swingy he can be. One really bad Profane Summons at the begining of the game will see you sing a far different tune.&nbsp;

LaCapitain is the same way at a lvl2 villain. Though she poses a more consistent threat than Apostate, Apostate at his worst is worse than Capitain at hers. Effigy + Orb is just about the last thing you wanna see.

